|>  	Why is it that sometimes when you are trying to memorize 
|> a spell from a spell book that it says -
|> You feel threatened -more
|> You can move again -more
|> And you lose the spell and nothing seems to happen.

Mostly because you have to be capable of learning the spell, and
even then there is only a random chance that you will learn it
THIS time you read it.  According to the Wheaton spoilers files,
there are other things which can happen to you, like you might
lose all your gold, or be teleported, etc. if you fail to
learn the spell.

Now, how can you tell if you are capable of learning the spell?
Well, the answer to that is a REAL spoiler, and I haven't
looked at the source to find out, but I suspect that its some
equation based on your level, the level of the spell you are
trying to learn, your intelligence, your luck, and the phase
of the moon B^)!

